  "grammar": [
    {
      "id": "b3_u09_l1_g1",
      "pattern": "N처럼",
      "meaning_uz": "...dek, ...kabi (o'xshatish)",
      "meaning_en": "Like N",
      "explanation_md": "**처럼** ot yoki olmoshga qo'shilib, **o'xshatish**ni bildiradi: \"**...dek**\", \"**...kabi**\".\n\n**가족처럼 지내는 친구들이 있어요.** — *Oiladek do'stlarim bor.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\n**처럼** 받침 ga qarab o'zgarmaydi: **가족처럼**, **천사처럼**, **엄마처럼**, **형제처럼**.\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- Ko'pincha **sifat yoki fe'l** oldidan: **천사처럼 착해요** (farishtadek mehribon), **한국 사람처럼 말해요** (koreysdek gapiradi).\n- Otdan oldin **같은** bilan: **가족 같은 친구** — *oiladek do'st*.\n- **N처럼 V** = **N 같이 V**: **가족같이 지내요** ham to'g'ri.\n- Maqtovda ko'p: **한국 사람처럼 한국어를 잘해요!**",
      "explanation_md_en": "**처럼** attaches to a noun or pronoun to make a **comparison**: \"**like N**\", \"**as … as N**\".\n\n**가족처럼 지내는 친구들이 있어요.** — *I have friends who are like family.*\n\n### How to form it\n\n**처럼** doesn't change with 받침: **가족처럼**, **천사처럼**, **엄마처럼**, **형제처럼**.\n\n### Remember\n\n- It usually comes **before an adjective or verb**: **천사처럼 착해요** (as kind as an angel), **한국 사람처럼 말해요** (speaks like a Korean).\n- Before a noun use **같은**: **가족 같은 친구** — *a friend who's like family*.\n- **N처럼 V** = **N 같이 V**: **가족같이 지내요** is also correct.\n- Common in compliments: **한국 사람처럼 한국어를 잘해요!**",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "Fe'l/sifatdan oldin",
          "condition_en": "Before a verb/adjective",
          "rule": "N처럼 + A/V",
          "example": "가족처럼 지내요, 천사처럼 착해요"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Otdan oldin",
          "condition_en": "Before a noun",
          "rule": "N 같은 + N",
          "example": "가족 같은 친구"
        }
      ],
