      ],
      "uz_compare": "O'zbekchadagi '-dek', '-day', '... kabi' ga mos: 'oilaDEK do'stlar' = 가족처럼 지내는 친구들, 'farishtaDEK mehribon' = 천사처럼 착해요.",
      "compare_en": "Like English 'like' or 'as … as': 'like family' = 가족처럼, 'as kind as an angel' = 천사처럼 착해요."
    },
    {
      "id": "b3_u09_l1_g2",
      "pattern": "A/V-겠-",
      "meaning_uz": "...sa kerak (taxmin, hamdardlik)",
      "meaning_en": "Must be … (guess, sympathy)",
      "explanation_md": "**-겠-** gapiruvchining **ko'rgan-eshitganiga asoslangan taxmini** yoki **hamdardligi**ni bildiradi: \"**...sa kerak**\", \"**...dirsiz**\". Ayniqsa suhbatdoshning holatiga munosabat bildirishda ko'p.\n\n**고향이 많이 그립겠어요.** — *Vataningizni ancha sog'ingandirsiz.*  \n**와, 맛있겠다!** — *Voy, mazali bo'lsa kerak!*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\n**-다** o'rniga **-겠어요** — 받침 ga qarab o'zgarmaydi:\n\n- 힘들다 → **힘들겠어요**, 피곤하다 → **피곤하겠어요**\n- 맛있다 → **맛있겠어요**, 외롭다 → **외롭겠어요**\n- O'tgan: **-았/었겠어요**: 힘들었겠어요 — *qiyin bo'lgan bo'lsa kerak*\n\n### Boshqa ma'nolari\n\n- **Rasmiy niyat** (4-1): **열심히 하겠습니다.** — *Tirishib ishlayman.*\n- **Tayyor iboralar**: **알겠습니다** (tushundim), **모르겠어요** (bilmayman), **잘 먹겠습니다**.\n\n### -(으)ㄹ 거예요 bilan farqi\n\n**-겠-** — hozir ko'rib turgan narsaga darhol munosabat: (taomni ko'rib) **맛있겠다!** **-(으)ㄹ 거예요** — umumiy taxmin.",
      "explanation_md_en": "**-겠-** expresses a **guess based on what you see or hear**, or **sympathy**: \"**must be**\", \"**that must …**\". It's very common when reacting to someone's situation.\n\n**고향이 많이 그립겠어요.** — *You must miss home a lot.*  \n**와, 맛있겠다!** — *Wow, that looks delicious!*\n\n### How to form it\n\nReplace **-다** with **-겠어요** — no change for 받침:\n\n- 힘들다 → **힘들겠어요**, 피곤하다 → **피곤하겠어요**\n- 맛있다 → **맛있겠어요**, 외롭다 → **외롭겠어요**\n- Past: **-았/었겠어요**: 힘들었겠어요 — *that must have been hard*\n\n### Other uses\n\n- **Formal intention** (4-1): **열심히 하겠습니다.** — *I'll do my best.*\n- **Set phrases**: **알겠습니다** (I understand), **모르겠어요** (I don't know), **잘 먹겠습니다**.\n\n### vs -(으)ㄹ 거예요\n\n**-겠-** reacts on the spot to what you see: (seeing the food) **맛있겠다!** **-(으)ㄹ 거예요** is a more general guess.",
      "formation": [
